# The parameter of a function that is handed out is proven nothing; the file's text writes two names. The read under the key was one generic operation: the turns ran other code, so the loop was built once and nothing in it
# was typed. Now each written name is compared with the key once, in front of the typed copy, behind the head's own question; the turn branches on the answers and reads the slot by name; who is none of the names begins the
# turn again in the closed copy, where the read stands as written.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: b0([[rows]]: {{*}}, [[key]]: anything
# RUN(HEADS): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# HEADS-COUNT-2: isLoopHead=true
# HEADS-NOT: isLoopHead=true
# RUN(EVENT): compile AccessesToldApartByTextsOfKey mechanisms=all
# EVENT: statistic AccessesToldApartByTextsOfKey 2
# RUN(TYPED): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# TYPED: : number @Double, {{*}} isInLoop=true isLoopHead=true
